#prompt {
    HTTP server. Register routes, then listen; listen serves requests until the program is stopped.

    A handler is a function taking one json, the request:
        { method, path, params: {name: value}, query: {name: value}, headers: {name: value}, body }
    body is the parsed JSON when the request is JSON, otherwise the text (empty string if none).
    Paths match exactly, except a segment written :name, which matches any one segment and appears
    in params. Header names are lowercase.

    What a handler returns becomes the response:
    - a string: 200, text/html if it starts with "<", otherwise text/plain
    - json, a list, a number or a bool: 200, application/json
    - the result of respond(status, body, headers): that status and headers, body as above
    A handler that throws gets a 500 with the error message as text. No route: 404, "not found".

    Each request is logged to stdout as "METHOD path → status".
}

flex native void get(string path, fn handler)
flex native void post(string path, fn handler)
flex native void put(string path, fn handler)
flex native void delete(string path, fn handler)
flex native json respond(int status, vibe body, json headers = {})
flex native void listen(int port = 8080)
